# Restart Helix after each iteration

When you change anything Helix loads at runtime — Python, `web/static/`, helper
scripts, or `workspace-template/` / `~/.helix/workspace` prompts — restart the
local process before you finish the turn.

1. From the repo root: `.\stop.ps1` then `.\start.ps1`
2. Confirm the admin UI answers on http://127.0.0.1:18791 (or the port in `~/.helix/config.json`)
3. Tell the user Helix was restarted

Do not skip this because chat.html or a workspace markdown file “does not need a restart”. Restart anyway so the running process matches the iteration.

Skip only when the turn made no Helix-facing change (pure Q&A, no edits).
